constructed
route: GET /pods/<pod>
status: 200
tack-sends: yes
built-from: pod-attended.json with the three keys a docket that lists `podContract` adds to a team's report: `delivers` (branch, report or records), `methods` (name, source, default, missingRoles) and `needs` (kind, name, fix, satisfied)
docket: not shipped; the keys Tack asked of docket's session on 2026-11-03 (ADR 0036 "What is asked of docket"), API 6, additive, announced in `features` as `podContract`
date: 2026-11-04
note: not captured, because no docket sends these keys yet; the keys are the ones Tack asked for and nothing else, and the values are made up. Tack reads them only when `GET /health` lists `podContract`. It replaces this file with a capture the day docket ships the feature.
